// Lesson 10 of 11 — Drums
// Preview: Ctrl+K V
//
// A drum part is written as patterns. `drums { }` plays its lines together —
// each a `phrase` or `{ … }` — and draws them as drummers read: hands on top,
// feet below. Hover a pattern's name to see its beat.
//
// STEP 1 — in bar 4, after `kick`: a space, then Ctrl+Space. The patterns come
// first. Pick `fillTriplet` — its `phrase` appears above.
// STEP 2 — in `groove`, replace `back` with `ghost` (Ctrl+Space shows it):
// a soft extra snare, drawn in parentheses.

title "Back Beat"
composer "Lily# lessons"

tempo 96

phrase hats   { hh8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 | }
phrase back   { r4 sn r sn | }
phrase kick   { bd4 r8 bd bd4 r | }
phrase groove { drums { hats back kick } }

part kit { clef percussion }

section A {
  kit {
    groove groove groove
    drums { kick }              // STEP 1: a fill goes here, beside the kick
  }
}

form { ~A }

score { staff kit }

// TRY: change `hh8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8` to `hh8 8 8 8 8 8 hho hh` — every bar that
// plays `hats` changes. `sn16@parenthesize` is a ghost note,
// `acciaccatura { sn16 } sn4` a flam.
//
// NEXT — type `lesson` on a new line and pick `lesson-11-band`.